@@ -0,0 +1,67 @@
+# Pi extension diagnostics: presentation
+
+Extension problems must read as a short, calm status, never as a log dump. This
+document inventories how they reach the screen, compares that with Pi 1.4.0 and
+records the rules the presentation now follows.
+
+## Paths to the screen
+
+| Source | Where | Before | Now |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Factory failed or skipped at start | adapter `lib/issues.mjs` -> `notification` | one `[Extension issues]` block: absolute path, 3-line reason, `Next:` per extension, no cap | one notice per severity, extension name, one line each, at most 4 lines |
+| Handler threw, was slow, unsupported field | `ExtensionIssues.callback/slow` | same block per event | same short line, once per (extension, event) per process |
+| Turn projection could not be converted | `ExtensionIssues.observation` | block with "octet could not convert the turn to Pi event data" | `<event> data was unavailable, so some activity was missed` |
+| Custom renderers inert | `inertRenderers` | lists renderer names | `custom display not shown; the default view is used` |
+| Background host-call failure | `runtime.backgroundError` | `Pi compatibility error` with up to 4096 bytes of raw error text, every time | first line, directories stripped, 160 chars, once per distinct text, max 32 |
+| Extension process did not start | host `lifecycle.rs`, `extensions.rs` | `extension X did not start: <whole stack trace> (see /extensions)` | one line: most informative line of the reason, directories dropped, 160 chars |
+| Queued extension action (`/reload`, `/extensions`, commands) | host `modes/interactive.rs` | `extension action queued for the next idle boundary; approval and eligibility are checked there` | `extension action queued; it runs when the current response finishes` |
+| Extension `ctx.ui.notify` | adapter `api.mjs` | verbatim, attributed | unchanged: the extension's own words, as in Pi |
+| Console output of extensions | adapter stderr -> host diagnostics | bounded, only in `/extensions` | unchanged |
+| Pi setup discovery diagnostics | `resources.mjs`, `runtime.mjs` | stderr (log) only | unchanged |
+
+## Pi 1.4.0 reference
+
+- Startup: one `[Extension issues]` heading, each entry `path` + message, with
+  paths shortened relative to the package.
+- A throwing event handler: `Extension "<path>" error: <message>` followed by
+  the dimmed stack, in the chat, every time it throws.
+- Reload while streaming is refused: `Wait for the current response to finish
+  before reloading.`
+
+octet deliberately does less per problem: no stack, no path, no repeat. It
+queues the reload instead of refusing it, and says when it will run.
+
+## Rules
+
+1. A chat notice names the extension (declared display name, else package, else
+   file name) and never a path, stack, error text or console output.
+2. One reason and one action per line; actions are imperative and pronoun-free
+   so a line can name several extensions ("A, B and 3 more: ...").
+3. Identical (reason, action) pairs merge; at most three names are shown.
+4. At most four lines per notice. Overflow ends with
+   `N more problems. See /extensions for details.`
+5. Severity is split: `error` means the extension was skipped; `warning` means
+   it still runs but degraded. Each is its own notice. When the host negotiated
+   `notification_source_v1` the label is `Pi extensions`; the host owns the
+   wording of the header.
+6. Repeats are suppressed per (extension, event) for the process lifetime and
+   per distinct text for background errors. The host additionally drops an
+   identical notice for 30 s.
+7. Details live in the log: every issue, with its path and the same reason, is
+   written to the adapter's stderr, which the host keeps in `/extensions`.
+8. Raw exception text never enters a notice: even an unsupported property name
+   can be prompt data. This is unchanged and still enforced by tests.
+
+## Host primitive
+
+`startup_failure_notice` in `extensions/composition.rs` is generic: it knows
+nothing about Pi. It keeps the most informative line of an arbitrary
+failure reason, drops directories, strips controls and bounds the length. All
+Pi wording stays in `lib/issues.mjs`.
+
+## Not changed
+
+Extension command failures returned as RPC errors (a command handler that
+throws) still show the extension's own message; it is bounded to 4096 bytes by
+the adapter and shown as a single error. Clipping those is a possible
+follow-up.
